---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'

// Account & data deletion.
//
// Google Play requires a PUBLIC web URL where a user can request account and
// data deletion — reachable without installing the app and without signing in,
// so someone who has deleted the app (or can't get into it) still has a route.
// In-app deletion alone does not satisfy that requirement; this page is the URL
// declared in Play Console -> Data safety.
//
// It documents both routes: the in-app one (immediate, self-service) and email
// (for anyone who can't reach the app). Content is grounded in what the
// delete-account Edge Function actually does — see union-supabase
// supabase/functions/delete-account/{orchestrator,service}.ts. If that
// behaviour changes, this page must change with it.

const toc = [
  { id: 'in-app', label: 'Delete it yourself' },
  { id: 'by-email', label: 'Ask us to delete it' },
  { id: 'what-goes', label: 'What gets deleted' },
  { id: 'partial', label: 'Deleting only some things' },
]
---

<Layout
  title="Delete your account"
  description="How to delete your Union account and the data associated with it."
>
  <Header back />

  <section class="title-block">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Your data</div>
      <h1>Delete your <em>account.</em></h1>
    </div>
    <dl class="meta">
      <dt>Email</dt>
      <dd><a href="mailto:privacy@unionwith.app">privacy@unionwith.app</a></dd>
      <dt>Deleted within</dt>
      <dd>Immediately in the app; 30 days by email</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
    <ul>
      {toc.map((t) => <li><a href={`#${t.id}`}>{t.label}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <section id="in-app">
    <h2>Delete it yourself, in the app</h2>
    <p>
      This is the quickest route, and it happens straight away — no waiting on
      us.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Open Union and go to <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
      <li>Scroll to <strong>Delete Account</strong>.</li>
      <li>Confirm. Your account and its data are removed immediately.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="aside">
      Deleting your account does not cancel a subscription bought through the
      App Store or Google Play — those are managed by the store, not by us. To
      stop future payments, cancel the subscription in your Apple or Google
      account settings as well.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="by-email">
    <h2>Ask us to delete it</h2>
    <p>
      If you no longer have the app installed, or you can't sign in, write to
      <a class="inline" href="mailto:privacy@unionwith.app"
        >privacy@unionwith.app</a
      > from the email address you used for Union, and ask us to delete your
      account.
    </p>
    <p>
      We'll confirm the request and delete the account within <strong
        >30 days</strong
      >. We ask from the registered address because it's the only way we can
      tell it's really your account — we won't delete an account on someone
      else's word.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="what-goes">
    <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
    <p>Deleting your account removes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your account and sign-in details</li>
      <li>Your journal entries, written and spoken</li>
      <li>Your voice recordings, including the stored audio files</li>
      <li>Prayers you wrote yourself</li>
      <li>Your saved prayers and verses</li>
      <li>Your check-ins and the prayers they suggested</li>
      <li>Your settings, including your tradition and reminder times</li>
      <li>Your notification tokens, so reminders stop</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Two things behave slightly differently, and we'd rather be plain about it:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Prayers you shared with someone.</strong> The links stop working
        and are no longer connected to you or your account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Records we're required to keep.</strong> Purchase and billing
        records held by Apple, Google or our payment provider are theirs, kept
        for tax and accounting reasons. We can delete your Union account without
        being able to erase their records.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="aside">
      Deletion is permanent. We can't recover a deleted account, and there's no
      grace period once it's confirmed in the app — so if you only want a break,
      signing out is the gentler option.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="partial">
    <h2>Deleting only some things</h2>
    <p>
      You don't have to delete everything to delete something. Inside the app you
      can remove a single journal entry, a prayer you wrote, a voice recording,
      or a saved prayer or verse, and you can retract a prayer you've shared so
      the link stops working. Your account stays as it is.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you'd like a copy of your data, or want something removed that you can't
      reach in the app, write to <a
        class="inline"
        href="mailto:privacy@unionwith.app">privacy@unionwith.app</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our <a class="inline" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains what we
      collect and why.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .aside {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
  ol,
  ul {
    margin: 0 0 1rem 1.1rem;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
</style>
